    "intro_html":  "Brown stew chicken is the other side of Jamaican cooking, the one that does not involve fire and allspice. You burn a little sugar in the pot until it goes dark, brown the chicken in it, then build a gravy around thyme, scallion, ketchup and bell pepper. Sweet, savory and deeply brown, which is exactly where the name comes from. Over rice, each bowl runs \u003cstrong\u003e579 calories and 35 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$1.08\u003c/strong\u003e.",
